      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Gentle parenting is often criticized for undermining the necessary structure children need to develop self-control and resilience. By avoiding firm boundaries, proponents of this style risk creating children who lack the ability to navigate real-world conflict. Furthermore, the focus on emotional validation can sometimes excuse poor behavior, teaching children that their feelings supersede the need for discipline. This approach, in essence, prioritizes comfort over character building, which is a fundamental failure in raising capable adults.",
